CORE
deep-let.smt2

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^unsat$
--
^\(error
--
Regression test for handling deeply nested input without unbounded recursion
anywhere in the pipeline. A deeply-nested chain of `(let ((xN xN-1)) ...)` of
depth 3500 is parsed and solved (unsat) without overflowing the call stack:
the SMT2 parser, expand_function_applications, the boolbvt let conversion and
irept destruction all avoid per-level recursion. A recursive implementation of
any of these stages segfaults on this input, including on the small (~1 MiB)
default stack used on some platforms (e.g. Visual Studio); the test is run as
CORE so those small-stack configurations are exercised.
